{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 39, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "The world shifted the moment Daniel opened his eyes. The sterile white walls of his bedroom dissolved into a pixelated expanse of blue sky and towering digital mountains, the air humming with the static of unseen code. He stumbled to his feet, his bare toes pressing into soft, unnaturally bouncy grass that glowed faintly beneath the sunlight. A status bar flickered at the corner of his vision—HP: 100%, MP: 50/50, Level: 1—and his reflection in a nearby stream revealed a crude, blocky avatar of himself, clad in a tunic of questionable taste. Panic clawed at his throat as he realized no one else seemed to notice the absurdity; a group of villagers in cartoony robes chattered nearby, completely oblivious to the man who had just materialized among them.\n\n***\n\nDaniel’s hands shook as he approached the villagers, their voices a blur of cheerful gibberish until one turned and asked, \"You new in town, traveler?\" in perfect, if slightly accented, English. Relief flooded him—some part of this world understood him—but terror followed when he noticed the quest log unfurling in his mind: *\"Slay the Bandit King in the Dark Forest to unlock the Warrior class.\"* He had no sword, no skills, just the nagging certainty that death in this place would be permanent. The villagers cheered him on, oblivious to his mounting dread, and as he stepped toward the ominous treeline, a notification flashed: *\"Tutorial: Combat Basics.\"* Resigned, he clenched his fists. If this was a game, he was going to play it—even if it meant learning to die spectacularly.", "logprobs": [{"token": "The", "logprob": -2.095531702041626}, {"token": " world", "logprob": -4.101406574249268}, {"token": " shifted", "logprob": -3.5048162937164307}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -1.7704473733901978}, {"token": " moment", "logprob": -0.027790136635303497}, {"token": " Daniel", "logprob": -